+### Wasmer
+
+With the "Deploy to Wasmer" button at the top of this README, Wasmer detects Next.js, installs dependencies with Yarn and builds with the project's `yarn build` script (`yarn mask && cross-env BUILD_MODE=standalone next build`). The button builds this public repository as-is and does not fork or copy it into your GitHub account; to customize NextChat and redeploy on every push (and to keep receiving upstream updates, see [Keep Updated](#keep-updated)), fork it and connect your fork from the Wasmer dashboard. Set secrets in the app's Settings → Environment Vars:
+
+- `OPENAI_API_KEY` (or another provider key such as `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`): required unless every user enters their own key in the settings page. The server currently prints the selected key to its logs, so keep the app's logs private.
+- `CODE`: comma-separated access passwords. Required whenever a provider key above is set: without it anyone who has the app URL can chat on your key.
+- `BASE_URL` (optional): an OpenAI-compatible endpoint instead of `https://api.openai.com`.
+- `DEFAULT_MODEL` (optional): the model selected by default.
+
+See [Environment Variables](#environment-variables) for the full list.
